In <22363@goanna.cs.rmit.oz.au> adam@arcadia.cs.rmit.EDU.AU (Adam Eberbach) writes:

>That's silly. Nobody is stupid enough to try to eat a T-rex corpse whole.
>IMHO the whole idea of choking to death without a question about whether you
>want to stop is silly.

I think even with the question choking is silly. A character  who
uses  weapons  and  magic  with reasonable skill and without ever
injuring himself doesn't choke to death that easily.
It would make much more sense to me if overeating had effects  of
decreasing  speed and dexterity. E.g. there could be a max. level
of satiation above which NH simply doesn't allow any more  eating
("You  cannot  stuff  anymore  into your stomach"). Then, a state
called "overfed" or something alike should  be  introduced  above
"satiated".  If a character is overfed, s/he is slowed down. If a
character is overfed over a prolonged period  of  time  (i.e.  if
s/he  keeps  eating stuff despite being overfed), the character's
dexterity should be decreased.

>Armor is not a body hugging item - there is usually a lot of space left
>over in a suit of armor. 

A minor point on wearing armor: I have difficulties understanding
why  armor being worn uses space in the knapsack, and I could use
some extra slots sometimes.
Also, cloaks etc. could have handy pockets inside  to  accomodate
small items, such as gems.

